    "html": "<p>A container holds a fixed mass of an ideal gas at pressure <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span>. The volume of the container is reduced to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2}\"></span> of its original value while the absolute temperature of the gas is tripled. What is the resulting pressure of the gas?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{3}{2}P\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2}{3}P\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"6P\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{6}P\"></span></p></li></ol>"
